   "title": "Downloads + requirements",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Downloads + requirements\n\nClick the file name to download it. Put it in the folder shown (inside `ComfyUI/models/`).\n\n| Folder | File (click = download) | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| `diffusion_models/` | [flux3-image-klein-int8-convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/flux-3-image-klein-comfy/resolve/main/diffusion_models/flux3-image-klein-int8-convrot.safetensors) | 5.8 GB |\n| `text_encoders/` | [qwen3vl_4b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/flux-3-image-klein-comfy/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_int8_convrot.safetensors) | 4.9 GB |\n| `vae/` | [flux2-vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/flux-3-image-klein-comfy/resolve/main/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors) | 0.3 GB |\n\nTotal 11.0 GB. The BFL repo is gated: log in on Hugging Face and accept the terms first.\n\n**VRAM:** ComfyUI stayed inside each budget it was given: 5.9 GiB peak at 6 GiB, 7.9 at 8, 10.8 at 12 (it fills what it gets). The model and the text encoder together are bigger than 6 GB, so ComfyUI keeps part of them in system RAM. RAM use was not measured.\n\n**ComfyUI 0.45.3** (FLUX 3 Image support came in 0.41). **No custom nodes.** GGUF files of Klein need the ComfyUI-GGUF custom node, so this file uses BFL's int8 file.\n\nLicence: FLUX 3 Image Klein is under the FLUX Kommunity License (non-commercial; commercial use of outputs only under US$5M revenue). Read the model page.\n"
   ]
  }
